& [OnlyNextSlice] is the anti-overwhelm work boundary
  + [deliverable] is a tiny executable SOP-RVM Core v0.1 reference
  + [scope] is the eight fixtures in SOP_Core.CoreAcceptance
  + [files_expected] is semantic IR schema, fixture corpus, evaluator skeleton, and fixture tests
  + [review_harness] is wrap the same eight fixtures with InferenceCapsule and ReviewProgram records without adding scope
  + [history_harness] is precede fixture material transitions with fixture-local PertinentHistoryReview records without selecting a database
  + [first_runnable_proof] is one machine-form fixture, in-memory state, deterministic mock provider, capsule review, revision, and append-only trace
  + [second_runnable_proof] is run the same fixture through an Ollama structured-output adapter after the mock passes
  + [third_runnable_proof] is serve one missing definition through fixture-local sop_lookup using exact, graph, and embedding retrieval
  + [graph_IR_proof] is represent one subject across definition, inference, contract, execution, and provenance projections with causal discrimination
  + [Cantor_proof] is resolve one perspective to digest-validated clauses in two fixture files, quote them to a mock provider, and survive line relocation
  + [Cantor_trust_proof] is accept only a test-signed compiled package and reject unsigned, modified, corrupted, revoked, mixed, downgraded, or scope-invalid authority
  + [lightest_runtime_proof] is one signed package, one slim primer, one sop_query tool, two staged queries, one operation, one contract, and one rejected unsigned dependency
  + [component_manifestation] is one local Cantor process containing the runtime kernel, trust gate, semantic fabric, query service, mock provider, review, and trace
  - never: begin deferred database, distributed model, faculty, geometry, or interface work inside this slice

